feat: v0.2 panel - the four browser screens

Adds the human-facing half the objective calls for: a workbench mounted into
the DSH centre column with a sidebar toggle, plus the host API it reads from.

Client (src/client/**, browser bundle):
- planner screen: output config (hero/detail counts, aspect, in-image
  language), analyze -> plan, the visual style guide, per-section generation
  and a whole-page job. Re-planning is behind an explicit confirmation because
  it deletes every section, version and generated image.
- editor screen: per-section preview, inline editing of
  title/goal/copy/visualPrompt, generate / regenerate / repaint / enhance /
  translate, and the version list with activate.
- xiaohongshu: the four-step carousel flow with per-page download.
- channels: diagnostics - active channel, model catalog, image/vision/text
  counts, per-channel key presence, and the quota-rotation note.

Host (src/host/routes.ts, src/shared/routes.ts):
- 23 routes under /api/dsh-mxpage/* registered on the webServer service, fenced
  to loopback, all using the { ok } / { ok:false, code, message } envelope.
- route paths live in src/shared/routes.ts so the browser bundle does not pull
  node:http or the webserver types in.

Build-format fix (a real bug, not a detail):
The DSH web shell does not load client halves as ESM. It hands each bundle a
window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id, factory }) facade plus a require that
resolves the shell's live module table. Shipping plain ESM would have meant the
panel silently never applied - no error, no surface. tsdown now emits the
browser half as CJS into lib/client.raw.cjs and scripts/wrap-client.mjs wraps it
into the envelope; test/client-bundle.test.ts loads the built bundle through a
simulated facade and asserts apply + inject come back.

Also: inject is now ['webServer'] (the panel API needs it at apply time), with
tools/attachments still pulled per-effect through ctx.inject so the plugin boots
even when a surface is missing.

Verified: tsc --noEmit 0 errors; 37 tests pass; lib/index.js 298 KB,
lib/client.js 113 KB with react/react-dom left external.
